.SH BUGS
The window, the clip and the position baseline come from a measurement with Qwen3-0.6B over the
tree's docs, man pages and C
.RB ( doc/words.md );
the bands' bounds and
.IR segment 's
penalty and least length are placeholders, set on
.IR lmsim 's
model of bytes; the real model's scores over the tree's text will set them.
.PP
A command with a chorded argument loses the argument when written back.
.PP
On acme alone, without
.IR amux (4),
a window that
.IR win (1)
or another program reads gets no events after the program ends: acme keeps one reader of
.BR event ,
and the program's read takes the other's place.
Under
.IR amux ,
Huh and Bits leave a window whose
.B event
another session holds, as
.IR win 's
does.
